    "body": "  Hi, I am using `teleproto` to listen for incoming Telegram channel messages via `NewMessage`, but I am seeing random receive delays.\n\n  ### Environment\n\n  - teleproto: `1.225.2`\n  - Node.js: `18.20.8`\n  - Session type: user `StringSession`\n  - API: `client.addEventHandler(..., new NewMessage({ incoming: true }))`\n\n  ### Usage\n\n  ```js\n  client.addEventHandler(\n    async (event) => {\n      const receivedAtMs = Date.now();\n      const message = event.message;\n\n      const messageTimeMs =\n        message.date instanceof Date\n          ? message.date.getTime()\n          : Number(message.date) * 1000;\n\n      console.log({\n        channel: event.chatId,\n        messageId: message.id,\n        messageTime: new Date(messageTimeMs).toISOString(),\n        receivedAt: new Date(receivedAtMs).toISOString(),\n        receiveDelayMs: receivedAtMs - messageTimeMs,\n      });\n    },\n    new NewMessage({ incoming: true })\n  );\n```\n\n\n  ### Problem\n\n  For some channels, receiveDelayMs is very small, usually under 1-2 seconds.\n\n  For other channels, messages are sometimes received with a much larger delay, around 10-20 seconds. The behavior is random: the same process/session may receive one channel almost immediately, while another channel is delayed by more than ten\n  seconds.\n\n  The delay is measured at the beginning of the event handler, comparing Date.now() with message.date, so it does not appear to be caused by downstream processing in my application.\n\n  ### Expected behavior\n\n  NewMessage events for monitored channels should be delivered as soon as Telegram sends the update, or at least the delay pattern should be explainable.\n\n  ### Questions\n\n  1. Is this delay expected behavior from Telegram channel updates, or could it be caused by teleproto update handling?\n  2. Can this happen when channel PTS has a gap and teleproto waits for / fetches updates.GetChannelDifference?\n  3. Is there a recommended way to debug whether a delayed message came from a real-time UpdateNewChannelMessage or from a later channel difference fetch?\n  4. Are there any settings or APIs to reduce this delay for channel message monitoring?\n\n  ### Notes\n\n  I noticed teleproto handles channel updates through UpdateNewChannelMessage and channel PTS tracking. I am trying to understand whether the random 10-20s delay is normal Telegram behavior, a connection/DC issue, or something in the update manager\n  buffering / difference recovery logic.",
